WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.776 --> 00:00:18.202
By July the gardens were thriving, and so were the children, who played outside from morning till night.

2
00:00:20.664 --> 00:00:26.329
One evening when Jo was getting Teddy ready for bed, he pointed excitedly to the window.

3
00:00:26.349 --> 00:00:28.691
"My Danny!"

4
00:00:29.251 --> 00:00:29.932
he cried.

5
00:00:31.836 --> 00:00:36.878
"No, honey, he's not there," Jo said, pulling Teddy's nightshirt over his head.

6
00:00:36.898 --> 00:00:39.740
"Danny at the window!"

7
00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:41.200
Teddy insisted.

8
00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.862
"I saw him, Mama!"

9
00:00:43.882 --> 00:00:49.724
"Maybe it was Dan," Jo thought, hurrying to the window.

10
00:00:50.525 --> 00:00:53.806
She called Dan's name, but there was no reply.

11
00:00:53.826 --> 00:00:57.648
"Come, Teddy, help me call Dan."

12
00:00:59.388 --> 00:01:02.270
Jo hoped that Dan might respond to Teddy's voice.

13
00:01:03.971 --> 00:01:09.895
But after a few minutes, both Jo and Teddy were disappointed that Dan did not appear.

14
00:01:12.517 --> 00:01:15.439
After Teddy fell asleep, Jo went downstairs.

15
00:01:18.201 --> 00:01:23.365
She decided her son had been mistaken, so she didn't bother her husband with the news.

16
00:01:24.986 --> 00:01:30.865
While the professor sat in his study, writing letters, Jo mended socks in her study next door.

17
00:01:32.685 --> 00:01:36.987
It was past ten o'clock when Jo rose to shut up the house for the night.

18
00:01:39.527 --> 00:01:43.809
As she paused at a window, something white caught her eye outside.

19
00:01:43.829 --> 00:01:49.650
"Nan has left her hat on one of the haystacks again," she thought.

20
00:01:52.291 --> 00:01:54.652
Jo sighed and went out to retrieve it.

21
00:01:56.352 --> 00:02:00.114
But as she got closer to the haystack, she drew in a breath.

22
00:02:01.614 --> 00:02:07.397
The white object was a shirt—and Dan was lying on the haystack fast asleep!

23
00:02:09.017 --> 00:02:15.540
Ragged, dirty, and thin, he had bandaged one foot with an old jacket while his other foot was

24
00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:17.561
bare. "Dan."

25
00:02:18.021 --> 00:02:20.862
Jo bent over Dan and gently called his name.

26
00:02:20.882 --> 00:02:25.664
"I've come home," Dan whispered with a sleepy smile.

27
00:02:27.012 --> 00:02:33.277
"I thought you would return," Jo replied kindly, "and I'm so glad to see you."

28
00:02:35.278 --> 00:02:39.521
At those words Dan's eyes flew open, and he sat up.

29
00:02:41.262 --> 00:02:47.827
His face hardened, and he said rudely, "I'm not staying—I only wanted to peek in as I passed

30
00:02:47.927 --> 00:02:51.269
by." "Why not come in, dear?"

31
00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:54.772
Jo said, her face clouding with disappointment.

32
00:02:56.236 --> 00:02:58.437
"Teddy saw you earlier at the window."

33
00:02:58.457 --> 00:03:05.342
"I didn't think you'd let me," Dan said, fumbling for his small bundle, ready to take off.

34
00:03:06.803 --> 00:03:13.687
"Maybe you were mistaken," Jo said, extending one hand to Dan and pointing to the house with the

35
00:03:13.787 --> 00:03:21.232
other. Taking a deep breath, Dan stood up and limped toward the house.

36
00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:26.577
"Mr. Bauer won't be happy when he hears I ran away from Mr.

37
00:03:26.637 --> 00:03:28.818
Page's school," he mumbled.

38
00:03:28.838 --> 00:03:34.441
"He already knows, and it won't make any difference to him," Jo said.

39
00:03:34.461 --> 00:03:37.642
"What happened to your foot?"

40
00:03:39.063 --> 00:03:44.045
"When I was climbing over a wall, a heavy stone fell on it, but I don't mind."

41
00:03:45.765 --> 00:03:50.787
Dan did his best to be brave, but Jo could see that every step hurt him.

42
00:03:53.008 --> 00:03:56.409
Once they reached her study, she brought him some food and drink.

43
00:03:58.090 --> 00:03:59.551
"Where have you been, Dan?"

44
00:03:59.951 --> 00:04:00.571
she asked.

45
00:04:00.591 --> 00:04:06.414
"Mr. Page was too strict, so I ran off more than a month ago.

46
00:04:08.054 --> 00:04:11.596
I joined a man on a boat, and then I worked for a farmer for a couple of

47
00:04:11.636 --> 00:04:15.677
weeks. But he wouldn't pay me, so I took off again."

48
00:04:15.697 --> 00:04:18.298
"How did you survive?"

49
00:04:18.719 --> 00:04:21.740
Jo asked, looking at him with pity in her eyes.

50
00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:29.282
"Folks gave me things to eat," Dan explained, "and I slept in barns."

51
00:04:31.083 --> 00:04:33.264
Jo was still puzzled about his return.

52
00:04:33.284 --> 00:04:38.246
"If you didn't come back to stay with us, why are you here?"

53
00:04:38.266 --> 00:04:46.550
"I wanted to see Teddy again—and you—before I returned to my old job in the city.

54
00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:50.852
I planned to be gone by morning, but you found me."

55
00:04:52.948 --> 00:04:54.109
"Are you sorry I did?"

56
00:04:54.609 --> 00:04:58.091
Jo asked, kneeling down to examine his injured foot.

57
00:04:59.152 --> 00:05:07.077
Dan stared at the ceiling and said quietly, "No, I wanted to stay, but I was afraid you—"

58
00:05:07.497 --> 00:05:08.177
"Oh, Dan!"

59
00:05:08.498 --> 00:05:09.438
Jo blurted out.

60
00:05:09.458 --> 00:05:12.660
"When did you hurt this poor foot?"

61
00:05:14.641 --> 00:05:15.642
"Three days ago."

62
00:05:15.662 --> 00:05:18.784
"Mr. Bauer must look at this at once!"

63
00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:24.282
Jo hurried to her husband's study, leaving the door to her own study ajar.

64
00:05:25.463 --> 00:05:28.084
Dan overheard her telling the professor of his arrival.

65
00:05:28.104 --> 00:05:33.667
"I didn't have the heart to scold him, Fritz, because it's obvious he wants us to take him

66
00:05:33.727 --> 00:05:34.968
back," Jo said.

67
00:05:34.988 --> 00:05:38.149
"But he's afraid you won't forgive him."

68
00:05:38.169 --> 00:05:42.371
"This proves we have a hold on the boy's heart.

69
00:05:42.811 --> 00:05:43.852
Of course I'll forgive him."

70
00:05:45.984 --> 00:05:51.728
Two tears rolled down Dan's dusty cheeks as he listened, but he quickly wiped them away.

71
00:05:51.748 --> 00:05:58.413
"You must be kind to Dan, no matter how gruff he seems," Jo warned her husband.

72
00:05:58.433 --> 00:06:04.637
"A quiet word and patience will help him, just as they used to help me."

73
00:06:04.657 --> 00:06:08.639
"I doubt you were ever like Dan!"

74
00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:10.941
Mr. Bauer said, laughing.

75
00:06:12.782 --> 00:06:17.529
As the Bauers entered Jo's study, Dan tried to stand up but couldn't.

76
00:06:17.549 --> 00:06:20.770
"So you like it here more than at Mr.

77
00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:23.450
Page's?" the professor said pleasantly.

78
00:06:23.470 --> 00:06:27.572
"Well, let's see if we can get along better this time."

79
00:06:29.472 --> 00:06:34.774
"Thank you, sir," said Dan, finding it easier to be polite than he'd expected.

80
00:06:36.694 --> 00:06:37.314
After Mr.

81
00:06:37.354 --> 00:06:42.696
Bauer bathed and bound up Dan's foot, he said they must call the doctor the next day.

82
00:06:44.796 --> 00:06:48.058
Jo prepared a bed for Dan, who quickly fell asleep.

83
00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:53.282
But he awoke in the middle of the night, moaning in pain.

84
00:06:57.345 --> 00:06:58.005
you all right?"

85
00:06:58.465 --> 00:07:00.427
Jo said, arriving at his bedside.

86
00:07:00.447 --> 00:07:05.710
"My foot hurts, but I didn't mean to wake you," Dan said.

87
00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:07.752
"That's all right."

88
00:07:09.693 --> 00:07:11.234
Jo smoothed his pillow.

89
00:07:12.575 --> 00:07:17.881
To her great surprise, Dan threw his arms around her neck and kissed her cheek.

90
00:07:17.901 --> 00:07:21.085
"Thank you for taking care of me, ma'am!"

91
00:07:22.587 --> 00:07:27.533
Touched by his words and actions, Jo realized that Dan was sorry.

92
00:07:27.553 --> 00:07:32.560
"You're my boy now," she said, giving him a hug.
